& [Fold01_IdentityBoundary] asks what is actually the same
  + [probe] distinguish request identity, operand identity, comparison scope, canonical sequence identity, root identity, and complete lineage identity
  + reconciliation_identity correlates one invocation only
  + each commitment_identity and assembly_identity correlates a lower invocation only
  + complete operand equality is used for current rederivation, not pair disposition
  + common root identity is relative-path role plus kind plus volume serial plus file ID
  + canonical sequence identity is encoding profile plus ordered digest value
  + complete lineage identity may differ while canonical sequence disposition remains Equal
  + [edge_equal_sequence_distinct_lineage] must remain Equal and retain unequal carriers when both are currently valid and comparably scoped
  + [edge_equal_digest_distinct_root] must fault at root scope even if a collision, fixture substitution, or future test seam makes digest text equal
  + [edge_equal_digest_distinct_limits] must fault at limits because equal observed values under unequal ceilings do not share one declared comparison scope
  + [finding] identity roles remain separate and no integer or digest representation substitutes for another

& [Fold02_LinguisticTruth] asks what the output can honestly say
  + [probe] attempt to rename Equal as stable, unchanged, same inventory, repeated, before-after equal, or quiescent
  + stable fails because no time relation is observed
  + unchanged fails because no earlier state is privileged and no change interval exists
  + same inventory is ambiguous between supplied sequence content and complete physical enumeration
  + repeated fails because two supplied values do not prove two acquisitions
  + before-after fails because argument position is not physical observation order
  + quiescent fails because process, descendant, writer, and snapshot evidence are absent
  + Equal succeeds only as equal comparable supplied canonical sequence commitments
  + Different succeeds only as unequal comparable supplied canonical sequence commitments
  + [edge_swapped_operands] preserves disposition and changes positional lineage without changing time because time is absent
  + [finding] closed vocabulary is not cosmetic; it is the primary guard against evidence-grade inflation

& [Fold03_AdversarialProvenance] asks how a caller could launder evidence
  + [probe_bare_digest] attacker supplies two copied strings detached from assemblies
    - denied because no bare overload exists
  + [probe_forged_carrier] attacker deserializes a chosen output
    - denied because prerequisite and reconciliation success types are Serialize-only with private fields
  + [probe_stale_carrier] future prerequisite semantics drift after an older carrier exists in memory
    - current complete rederivation detects contradiction or failure before scope
  + [probe_cross_root] two different root identities happen to expose equal content
    - exact root scope rejects
  + [probe_weaker_limits] one operand used smaller declared ceilings but observed the same entries
    - exact complete limit equality rejects
  + [probe_correlation_swap] attacker changes caller correlation identities
    - correlation changes remain lineage and do not counterfeit or defeat semantic equality
  + [probe_argument_label] caller calls left before and right after in surrounding prose
    - this module still releases only positional roles and supplies no temporal evidence
  + [finding] output-only input, current rederivation, and scope-before-disposition form a three-gate provenance defense

& [Fold04_DataOwnershipAndCardinality] asks what must be owned and counted
  + [probe] compare borrowed values and return a detached enum
    - rejected because proof lineage would not accompany the disposition
  + exactly one plan and exactly two operands enter
  + exactly one common-scope record and one disposition leave beside both owned operands
  + no operand is dropped, merged, sorted, normalized, or reconstructed
  + cloning occurs only to feed current rederivation while original values remain available for eventual owned output
  + root extraction reads exactly the first validated member from each assembly
  + no full member traversal is needed beyond prerequisite digest rederivation
  + no new sequence, canonical-byte buffer, digest buffer, map, set, database row, or persistent state is created
  + [edge_large_valid_inventory] memory growth is bounded by two prerequisite clones already bounded by TopologyScanLimits and required for current complete rederivation
  + [edge_zero_or_three_operands] absent at the type signature rather than dynamically repaired
  + [finding] by-value two-carrier ownership is the smallest self-contained inspectable proof object

& [Fold05_FaultAndControlFlow] asks whether every branch has one meaning
  + [probe] enumerate plan, left, right, profile, limits, root, disposition, resource, and internal transitions
  + plan faults occur before any operand clone or rederivation
  + left failure prevents right work and preserves left nested fault
  + right failure occurs only after left success and preserves right nested fault
  + profile mismatch prevents limits and root comparison
  + limit mismatch prevents root and digest comparison
  + root structural or strong identity mismatch prevents digest comparison
  + digest equality releases Equal
  + digest inequality releases Different
  + Different is never routed into error control flow
  + every fault returns no common scope, disposition, or operand echo
  + diagnostic text is scalar bounded and excludes sensitive record values
  + [edge_impossible_empty_assembly] if future prerequisite evolution exposes it, root-scope or internal fault closes rather than indexing unsafely
  + [finding] deterministic precedence makes one failure explain the earliest unsatisfied truth condition

& [Fold06_EffectAndThreatSurface] asks what execution can change or observe
  + [probe] trace every required operation
  + plan byte length reads caller memory only
  + JSON decode allocates bounded in-process values only
  + operand clone reads supplied memory only
  + prerequisite digest rederivation performs validated in-memory hashing only
  + profile, limit, root, and digest comparisons read in-memory values only
  + result construction moves owned values only
  + no filesystem, path resolution, Windows, handle, pointer, unsafe, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, Git, model, tool, fixture, mutation, seal, cleanup, or promotion call is required
  + no physical test or effect-bearing evidence builder is needed for proportional proof
  + [edge_denial_of_service] plan is byte bounded and operand size inherits signed scan limits; faults remain bounded
  + [edge_side_channel_claim] timing is neither read nor returned, so elapsed behavior cannot become evidence
  + [finding] effect grade is pure deterministic supplied-value transformation with zero new dependency

& [Fold07_EvolutionAndCompatibility] asks how the boundary fails under change
  + [probe_profile_revision] either digest or encoding profile changes
    - exact current profile checks fault; no implicit migration
  + [probe_limits_revision] TopologyScanLimits adds a field with Eq semantics
    - complete equality naturally incorporates it, while canonical review must re-sign compilation compatibility
  + [probe_root_identity_revision] strong root identity meaning changes
    - current prerequisite hash/signature or source binding invalidates this authority
  + [probe_digest_type_revision] fields or equality semantics change
    - canonical hashes, static tests, current rederivation, and compilation gates expose drift
  + [probe_new_physical_wrapper] future code wants before-after semantics
    - must preserve new source and bind actual acquisitions; it may consume but not rewrite this output
  + [probe_first_difference_demand] diagnostics later require exact changed fields
    - new source is required because the current digest-only disposition intentionally does not authorize it
  + [probe_rollback] removing one module, export, tests, evidence, and closure records leaves all prerequisites intact
  + [finding] exact profiles and source binding make evolution fail closed rather than silently changing meaning

& [CrossFoldConvergence] is explicit
  + Fold01 identity separation requires the same common-scope record defended by Fold03 and owned by Fold04
  + Fold02 vocabulary guard is enforced by Fold05 result branches and Fold06 absence of time or physical effects
  + Fold03 current rederivation is feasible under Fold04 ownership and deterministic under Fold05 precedence
  + Fold04 complete lineage makes Fold02 claims inspectable without widening Fold06 effects
  + Fold05 Different-as-result preserves Fold01 sequence identity and avoids the policy confusion rejected by pruning
  + Fold06 zero-effect boundary is stable under the exact-profile evolution strategy in Fold07
  + Fold07 separate future physical wrapper preserves every prohibition found by Folds02, 03, and 06

& [ResidualQuestions] are dispositioned
  + [Q1_should_full_root_observation_equal] no because mutable committed root fields are legitimate sequence difference
  + [Q2_should_correlation_identities_equal] no because they are retained workflow provenance, not pair subject
  + [Q3_should_digest_text_be_revalidated_as_hex] predecessor output-only and complete rederivation already perform exact validation; duplicate decoder is unnecessary
  + [Q4_should_comparison_use_constant_time] no secret-bearing authentication claim exists and adding a security primitive would imply a different threat model
